<title>NORWAY: Fountain awards Ukraine deal to Croatian driller.</title>
<headline>Fountain awards Ukraine deal to Croatian driller.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fountain Oil has awarded a $1.2 million contract to Croatian drilling contractor INA Naftaplin for the recompletion of 12 existing wells on the Lelyaky oilfield in Ukraine, the company said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>Operator of the field is Ukraine-registered Kashtan Petroleum Ltd, in which Fountain holds a 40.5 percent stake. Ukranafta, the Ukrainian state oil company, has a 55 percent interest.</p>
<p>Recompletion work is scheduled to begin in December, with each well taking 15 days to complete, Fountain said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
